<section id="score-review" aria-labelledby="score-title">
<h3 id="score-title">Expected scores · matched margin and total heads</h3>
<p id="score-status" class="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">No expected-score projection inventory supplied. Missing pairs are not filled from other model rows.</p>
<p class="note">These are fractional expected home/away scores supplied by the owner from an exactly matched margin/total pair. They are not rounded outcome predictions, a new score model, an integer score distribution or a line-conditioned probability. No fit, immutable issue or promotion is created by displaying the derived means. Unsupported selected, meta-model or ensemble pairing stays explicit.</p>
<div id="score-content" hidden><p id="score-contexts" class="note"></p>
<div class="data-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Expected-score disposition</th><th>Emitted rows</th></tr></thead><tbody id="score-counts"></tbody></table></div>
<div class="toolbar"><div class="control"><label for="score-state">Loaded score-pair disposition</label><select id="score-state"><option value="all">Every supplied disposition</option></select></div><div class="control"><label for="score-league">Loaded score-pair league</label><select id="score-league"><option value="all">All supplied rows; leagues kept separate</option><option value="ncaam">Men</option><option value="ncaaw">Women</option><option value="unavailable">League unavailable in source disposition</option></select></div><div class="control search"><label for="score-search">Source ID, team, family or missing-input reason</label><input id="score-search" type="search" placeholder="Search the loaded score part"></div></div>
<div class="buttons"><button id="score-inspect" class="secondary" type="button">Inspect expected scores</button><button id="score-reset" class="secondary" type="button">Show all loaded score rows</button></div>
<p class="note">Select the named gzip part below. Its cards retain both original target prediction IDs, ordered teams, cutoff, origin, horizon and model context. These controls and the evidence-track selector affect only the loaded part. A missing name is shown by its exact supplied team ID; no alias is inferred.</p>
</div></section>
